{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c2ebf2f8be4f385ce268a895cee811cb5f67eda1b3e429169c11e509cdaf57b3","digest":{"component_or_area":"store initialization and marker management","key_entities":["*/.archived","*/.write.lock","rebar._store.ensures.REGISTRY_IDS","rebar._commands.init","reducer/_api.py","reducer/marker.py","rebar/_store/ensures.py","untrack-runtime-markers","git ls-files","git rm --cached","write_marker","exclude_archived"],"problem_keywords":["git tracking","runtime markers","gitignore","archive","write lock","ensure unit","self-healing cache","idempotent convergence"],"propositions":["Tracked */.archived and */.write.lock files in the tickets branch HEAD cause git status to show dirty state and break strict head checks in plan_review/relation_snapshot.py.","Runtime marker files should be untracked from git via a new ensure unit that uses git rm --cached and commits once, while leaving worktree copies intact.","Peers merging the untrack commit will have their worktree marker files deleted by git, requiring reader self-healing to re-materialize .archived markers for archived tickets on subsequent list operations.","The ensure unit check runs git ls-files to detect tracked markers (idempotent: second run commits nothing), and the act phase batches git rm --cached calls to avoid ARG_MAX limits."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787400439530519001,"uuid":"db4df2b6-a6ea-4062-918a-a66c0b7412dd"}